cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Large totient fibers (Erdős Problem 821), in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of OpenAI's theorem that for every epsilon > 0 there
  are infinitely many n with more than n^(1 - epsilon) solutions m of
  phi(m) = n (Erdős Problem 821), stated as Erdos821.erdos_821, together with
  the smooth shifted-prime theorem it is derived from. The final theorem uses
  only the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.
authors:
